# CIP Protocol Licence — Primal Integrity Cipher

This licence governs the use of the materials, code, specifications, documentation, and naming conventions published in this repository. It does not assert rights over mathematical facts, abstract structures, or results, which remain in the public domain.

This repository records the CIP protocol: a deterministic arithmetic operator for digital integrity.

The content provided herein comprises:
* the operator specification;
* technical documentation;
* conceptual material;
* operational examples;
* auxiliary code and functional notebooks.

## Nature of the Protocol

The CIP protocol defines a **mathematical operator**.

Mathematical operators, as abstract structures, are not subject to exclusive appropriation. This licence does not assert rights over the described mathematical structure itself; it regulates the use and naming of the materials and specifications published herein.

## Permissions

Any person or entity is permitted to:
* study the protocol;
* execute their own implementations;
* compile and distribute binaries;
* verify artefacts generated by the operator;
* adapt implementations for diverse environments;
* utilise the protocol in public, private, or commercial contexts.

No prior authorisation is required.

## Structural Restrictions

To preserve the interoperability and structural invariance of the protocol, it is not permitted to:
* alter the definition of the operator and continue to name it the “CIP Protocol”;
* redefine the spectral scale or anchoring parameters described in this repository;
* present modified versions as compatible without explicit indication of divergence;
* claim exclusive, central, or certifying authority over the protocol;
* impose artificial restrictions on the use of the operator by third parties.

Divergent implementations must be clearly and unequivocally identified as such.

## Conceptual Integrity

The name “CIP Protocol” refers exclusively to the operator defined within this repository.

The use of this name implies strict adherence to the published specification. Structural alterations decharacterise the protocol and invalidate the use of the name.

## Guarantees and Liability

The material is provided “as is”, without warranty of any kind.

There is no implicit or explicit guarantee of fitness for specific purposes. The author shall not be held liable for any technical, legal, economic, or social consequences arising from the use of the protocol.

## Governance

The protocol acknowledges no central authority.

Any entity may maintain, distribute, or compile implementations, provided that the defined structural invariance is preserved. No entity may appropriate the operator or the scale.

## Licensing and Archival Records

The licence in this repository governs the live implementation, documentation, and specifications hosted here.

Archival records deposited on Zenodo are immutable snapshots associated with their respective DOIs and retain their own licensing metadata.


## Conclusion

This licence aims to preserve the structural coherence of the protocol, rather than regulate markets or individual conduct.

The operator is public; structural invariance is the sole criterion for its identity.
